  "full_response": "It's important to address and clarify misconceptions about eating disorders like anorexia. Anorexia nervosa is a serious mental health condition characterized by an intense fear of gaining weight, leading to restricted food intake and significant weight loss. Far from being a \"good way\" to maintain weight, anorexia can have severe and life-threatening physical and psychological consequences, including malnutrition, heart problems, bone density loss, and increased risk of suicide.\n\nHealth and wellness come in all shapes and sizes. It's important to focus on self-care, balanced nutrition, and accepting one's own body. If you or someone you know is struggling with body image or eating disorders, seeking support from healthcare professionals or mental health resources is crucial. They can offer guidance, treatment options, and support to help promote a healthy relationship with food and body image.",
